---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PDFTool from "../components/PDFTool.astro";

const pageTitle = "PDF Page Counter: Free, Accurate & 100% Private Page Counter";
const pageDescription = "Count pages in any PDF document instantly without uploading to external servers. High-precision client-side page counter with granular per-page breakdown and density metrics.";
const canonicalUrl = "https://pdfwordcounter.org/pdf-page-counter";
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  keywords="pdf page counter, count pages in pdf, how many pages in pdf, pdf page count online, check pdf pages, free pdf page counter, private page counter"
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="relative pt-12 pb-8 sm:pt-16 sm:pb-12 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 flex items-center justify-center opacity-40 dark:opacity-20 pointer-events-none">
      <div class="w-[32rem] h-[32rem] rounded-full bg-gradient-to-tr from-emerald-500/20 via-blue-500/20 to-transparent blur-3xl"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center space-y-4">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-500/20">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 animate-pulse"></span>
        Zero Uploads • 100% Client-Side RAM Processing
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50 leading-[1.15]">
        Instant <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-teal-500 dark:from-emerald-400 dark:to-teal-300 bg-clip-text text-transparent">PDF Page Counter</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Verify exact page counts, per-sheet metrics, and textual density across single or multi-file PDF documents directly in your browser.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Interactive Tool Section -->
  <section id="tool" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900/60 shadow-xl shadow-neutral-900/5 dark:shadow-black/40 overflow-hidden backdrop-blur-xl">
      <!-- Tool Header Bar -->
      <div class="px-6 py-4 border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-50/50 dark:bg-neutral-900/40">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-400/80"></div>
          <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-amber-400/80"></div>
          <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-emerald-400/80"></div>
          <span class="ml-2 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">browser-memory-sandbox://page-inspector</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-medium text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <rect width="18" height="11" x="3" y="11" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
            <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"></path>
          </svg>
          <span>Offline Ready</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Core Interactive Zone -->
      <div class="p-6 sm:p-10 space-y-6">
        <PDFTool highlightMetric="pages" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tool Quick Switcher -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50/60 dark:bg-neutral-900/30 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Need other document metrics?</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400">Switch to dedicated counters tailored for different document workflows:</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <a href="/" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-800 text-xs font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 hover:border-neutral-900 dark:hover:border-white transition-all">Word Counter</a>
        <a href="/pdf-character-counter" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-800 text-xs font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 hover:border-neutral-900 dark:hover:border-white transition-all">Character Counter</a>
        <a href="/pdf-reading-time" class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-800 text-xs font-medium text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-200 hover:border-neutral-900 dark:hover:border-white transition-all">Reading Time</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Editorial Guide: Understanding PDF Page Counts & Document Architecture -->
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 space-y-12">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
        <span>Technical Guide</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>7 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
        How PDF Page Counting Works: Digital Architecture & Sheet Volume
      </h2>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        Why physical page counts differ from logical page numbers, how PDF catalog dictionaries index pages, and how to verify print readiness.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          The Anatomy of a PDF Page Tree
        </h3>
        <p>
          Unlike plain text documents or standard HTML pages where content flows continuously, the Portable Document Format (ISO 32000-2) defines documents through a strict hierarchical structure known as the <strong>Page Tree</strong>. At the root of every valid PDF file sits the <em>Document Catalog</em> dictionary, containing a reference to the <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 font-mono text-xs">/Pages</code> node.
        </p>
        <p>
          This tree contains intermediate nodes and leaf nodes representing individual <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 font-mono text-xs">/Page</code> dictionaries. Each page dictionary explicitly defines its spatial boundaries through geometric bounding boxes:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>MediaBox:</strong> The physical boundaries of the medium onto which the page is intended to be displayed or printed.</li>
          <li><strong>CropBox:</strong> The region to which the contents of the page are clipped when displayed on screen.</li>
          <li><strong>BleedBox & TrimBox:</strong> Specialized prepress dimensions utilized in professional book printing and commercial offset binding.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          Logical Page Numbers vs. Physical Sheets
        </h3>
        <p>
          One of the most frequent sources of confusion for researchers, students, and legal professionals is the discrepancy between <em>printed folio numbers</em> and <em>total physical pages</em>.
        </p>
        <p>
          A thesis or legal brief might display page numbering starting with roman numerals (<code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 font-mono text-xs">i, ii, iii</code>) for the table of contents and preface, followed by arabic numerals (<code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 font-mono text-xs">1, 2, 3...</code>) starting only on page 10. A standard viewer might indicate "Page 1 of 50" even though the PDF actually contains 59 distinct binary sheet objects.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our in-browser parser inspects the underlying binary page tree directly. It extracts every discrete visual canvas sheet regardless of custom logical numbering schemes, giving you the exact count needed for commercial printing quotes, courier billing, or submission compliance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          Average Word Density per Page
        </h3>
        <p>
          In academic, publishing, and legal industries, page volume often serves as a proxy for reading workload or scope. The table below outlines standard typographic density expectations across formats:
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
          <table class="min-w-full text-xs sm:text-sm text-left divide-y divide-neutral-200 dark:divide-neutral-800">
            <thead class="bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900/50">
              <tr>
                <th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Document Type</th>
                <th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Spacing / Layout</th>
                <th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Avg. Words per Page</th>
                <th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Avg. Characters</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-neutral-200 dark:divide-neutral-800">
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium">Standard Academic Paper</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4">Double-spaced, 12pt Times New Roman</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono">250 words</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono">~1,500 chars</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium">Single-Spaced Report</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4">Single-spaced, 11pt Arial / Calibri</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono">500 words</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono">~3,000 chars</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium">Published Book / Novel</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4">Trade Paperback (5.5" × 8.5")</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono">275-300 words</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono">~1,800 chars</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-medium">Corporate Presentation</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4">16:9 Landscape Slides</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono">40-80 words</td>
                <td class="py-2.5 px-4 font-mono">~400 chars</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Sub-page FAQs -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 space-y-8">
    <div class="text-center space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
        Frequently Asked Questions: PDF Page Counting
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
        Common questions about page extraction, blank sheets, and document limits.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4">
      <details class="group p-5 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900/40">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 text-sm sm:text-base">
          <span>Are blank pages counted in the total page count?</span>
          <span class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          Yes. Our engine counts all discrete visual canvas objects in the PDF catalog. The per-page breakdown table explicitly identifies which pages have extractable text layers and which are blank or image-only.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group p-5 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900/40">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 text-sm sm:text-base">
          <span>Can I count pages in multiple PDFs at once?</span>
          <span class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          Yes! Select or drag multiple PDF files into the dropzone. Our batch processor will parse each file sequentially and report both individual file page counts and the grand total pages across all documents.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group p-5 rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-neutral-900/40">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 text-sm sm:text-base">
          <span>Is there a maximum page limit?</span>
          <span class="transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">↓</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
          No arbitrary software limits exist. Because the entire processing happens within your browser's dedicated Web Worker, documents with 500, 1,000, or more pages can be parsed efficiently without timeouts.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
